  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Bakery Cottage",
    "description": "A remix of \"The One-Room Cottage\" by forkbuild: the one-room cottage becomes the village bakehouse. The walls, door, windows and hip roof are the cottage's own; inside, the hearth is now the bread oven, and out front a porch under a yellow awning is where the loaves are sold. 43 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Floor**: the cottage's wooden Slab 4x4.\n2. **Walls**: the cottage's Wall 2x3 panels and four dark corner Posts, unchanged.\n3. **Door and windows**: the cottage's Door, Window Frame and Large Window, unchanged.\n4. **Roof**: the Hip Roof 6x6, with a stone-grey Chimney over the oven.\n5. **Bakehouse**: the Hearth, now stone grey, is the bread oven against the back wall. The bed is gone: in its place two Shelves stand against the west wall as bread racks, a third is by the front wall, and a Table in the middle is the kneading counter, lit by a Lantern. A flour Barrel waits beside the oven.\n6. **Porch**: a second wooden Slab 4x4 in front of the door. Two Posts and a Beam hold up a yellow Slab 4x4 awning, which tucks under the roof's eaves. A Bench sits against the front wall, the rain Barrel moves to the porch's corner, and a Table with a Lantern on it is the bread stall.\n7. **Yard**: three Logs stacked against the west wall feed the oven, two Bushes flank the porch, and a Pine Tree stands behind the bakery.\n\n## Room to bake\n\nThe east half of the room is kept clear from the door to the oven, 2 wide, as in the cottage. The counter, racks and flour stand in the west half, so the baker walks in through the door straight to the oven. The awning is 3.5 above the porch, so a visitor stands under it at the stall.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Floor: 1 Slab 4x4\n- Walls: 6 Wall 2x3, 4 Post\n- Door and windows: 1 Door, 3 Wall 1x1, 1 Window Frame, 1 Low Wall 2x1, 1 Large Window, 1 Short Beam\n- Roof: 1 Hip Roof 6x6, 1 Chimney\n- Bakehouse: 1 Hearth, 1 Table, 1 Lantern, 3 Shelf, 1 Barrel\n- Porch: 2 Slab 4x4, 2 Post, 1 Beam, 1 Bench, 1 Table, 1 Lantern, 1 Barrel\n- Yard: 3 Log, 2 Bush, 1 Pine Tree\n\n43 bricks in all.\n\n## Credits\n\nRemixed from \"The One-Room Cottage\" by forkbuild, licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0. This remix is shared under the same license, CC-BY-SA-4.0.",
